Regarding anonymous ftp sites for binaries, I am happy to offer
my NeXT: mrcnext.cso.uiuc.edu 128.174.73.105.  I already have
PC Nethack 3.0 patchlevel 3 from Kevin Smolkowski (works ok except
the kick code doesn't understand the hjklyubn directions even with
number_pad off).

I will also keep a copy of the Mac version if someone can get a copy to me.

Our directory structure is broken up by system type so the pc binary
is in pc/nethack, and when I get a mac version it'll be in mac/nethack.

I'm also willing to snail mail disks for those who can't ftp.  (I'll
not email text encoded copies, but Kevin (kevins@cie.uoregon.edu) will
for those who want to get it that way.

If you want to get a copy via U.S. mail either send me a postage paid
return mailer with blank formatted disk(s) or why pay the extra postage
to send me a mailer and disk, just send a return address label (with
your address on it :-) and a check (or cash if you trust it in mail)
to cover the cost of disk(s) and a mailer and postage.  
Here is about what I pay for stuff:
25 cents for the mailer
50 cents for a 720K 3.5" disk, or a 1.2M 5 1/4" disk
25 cents for a 360K 5 1/4" disk
I haven't gone to the post office lately, but 75 cents should cover
the postage for one or two disks.
In pkzip version 1.02 format, the entire set of the 540K NETHACK.EXE
file and related files necessary to run compress to about 320K so
will fit on one of any type of disk.

Please send these requests to my home address.  I will also do Mac disks
when I get a copy in Mac format.  Requests for source will only be honored
in PC formats (I don't feel like running Stuffit as well as zip on them all) 
and I'll send whatever source I have for the version I'm running including
my options and edits for a NeXT which should be easy enough to bring back
to original as any changed file usually also has a *.old version that was 
the original.

 
